---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import TechBadge from '../components/TechBadge.astro';
import ProductLinks from '../components/ProductLinks.astro';
---

<MainLayout title="Overview">
  <section class="border-b border-zinc-800 pb-6 mb-6">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
      <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-wider text-sky-400 bg-sky-500/10 border border-sky-500/20 px-2 py-0.5 rounded uppercase">
        Science Fair Project 2026
      </span>
      <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-zinc-500">Autonomous Robotics &bull; 18-DOF Hexapod</span>
    </div>
    
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-100 mb-3">
      Low-Cost Multimodal AI Spider Robot
    </h1>
    
    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      An 18-degree-of-freedom hexapod robot engineered with accessible commodity hardware, real-time FreeRTOS dual-core embedded kinematics, and an embodied voice/vision AI reasoning loop powered by Llama 3.3 and Whisper.
    </p>
    
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mb-2">
      <TechBadge text="18x Micro Servos" />
      <TechBadge text="Dual-Core ESP32-S3 (100Hz IK)" />
      <TechBadge text="Raspberry Pi 4 AI Gateway" />
      <TechBadge text="ESP32-CAM MJPEG Video" />
      <TechBadge text="Omniroute Multimodal API Router" />
      <TechBadge text="React & Plotly 3D Web Twin" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Open-Source Product Hub Banner -->
  <ProductLinks />

  <!-- Quick Entry into Full Documentation Tree -->
  <div class="border border-sky-500/30 bg-sky-950/20 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
    <div>
      <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-sky-400 uppercase font-bold">// COMPREHENSIVE_REFERENCE</span>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-100 mt-0.5">Explore Full Technical Documentation</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 font-sans mt-1">Read the complete technical architecture, FreeRTOS pinout matrices, and IK derivations.</p>
    </div>
    <a
      href="/docs/01-system-overview"
      class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-sky-500 text-zinc-950 font-mono text-xs font-bold hover:bg-sky-400 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap"
    >
      Open Tech Docs &rarr;
    </a>
  </div>

  <!-- Aim & Results Grid -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
    <div class="border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 rounded-xl p-4 flex flex-col">
      <div class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-400 mb-2">// 01_PROJECT_AIM</div>
      <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-zinc-100 mb-2">Why We Built This</h2>
      <div class="text-xs text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed space-y-2 flex-grow font-sans">
        <p>
          Emergency search-and-rescue teams often face dangerous rubble, collapsed buildings, and hazardous material spills where wheeled rovers get stuck. Commercial multi-legged robots cost thousands of dollars.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our goal was to design an open, low-cost 18-DOF hexapod robot that traverses complex terrain and responds to natural voice instructions like <em>"Hey Spider, walk forward and inspect for obstacles"</em>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 rounded-xl p-4 flex flex-col">
      <div class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-sky-400 mb-2">// 02_THE_RESULT</div>
      <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-zinc-100 mb-2">What We Achieved & Learned</h2>
      <div class="text-xs text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed space-y-2 flex-grow font-sans">
        <p>
          <strong>What Worked:</strong> We successfully built and validated all 18 revolute motor joints, an analytical 100 Hz IK solver on FreeRTOS, live 1-to-N video relays, and an embodied LLM voice agent.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Key Limitation:</strong> Full payload mass reached 1,310g (4.15 kg·cm torque demand), exceeding the continuous thermal limits of budget micro-gear servos. The system is presented on a custom DTC testing stand with external 5.3V power to demonstrate all 18-DOF motion and AI pipelines safely.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>